The Observers are a pair of beings that watch the world from behind a wall on a floor that does not exist, reached through the slip that opens from a rector's house. They are eyestalk beings, upright and curt, and the Weft are careful never to call them beholders. Only two of them were there when the Weft came through, and they were not at full strength.

They are the counterpart to [[Divinity/The Narrative/index|the Narrative]]. There are three observation spots, and a third Observer once stood with them. That one is gone, and [[Divinity/Immix|Immix]] had taken its place; the Observers would not say how or why it came to hold the spot, and would say only that the matter was between them and Immix. With Immix dead the spot stands open again. The pair will not share what they know without a trade, and can be paid in things as good as a wish.

The Weft traded them a divine wish and the Luck Blade, which vanished into a burst of light of a colour none of them could name. In return they promised to hunt down and kill whoever next wronged the pair, if they were able, a favour the Observers mean to call in. Chains of that same wrong colour wrapped the four and faded from sight, still faintly felt, and hamper nothing. [[People/Althane/The Broker|Tech]], who was not party to the deal, took no chain and did not watch. For the trade the Observers let the Weft watch an echo of [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|Vesper Feep]]'s life, and by that watching his name came to them.
